e + fee) for a list. Fits. **Kept.**\n- `BASE_PREMIUM` → **Renamed to `MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM`**. With the addition of `COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM`, the generic name `BASE_PREMIUM` no longer revealed *which* base premium it holds. The new name makes the main-item vs. component distinction explicit and symmetric with `COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM`.\n\n### Step 2 & 3: Structural improvement (Rule 2 — Reveals Intent)\n- Moved `interface`/type declarations to the **top of the file**, before the constants and functions that consume them. Intent is now revealed before use; the reader sees the data shapes first.\n- Grouped related constants logically: policy-level fees (`PROCESSING_FEE`, `FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE`) together, then the premium lookups (`COMPONENT_*`, `MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM`) adjacent to the `itemBasePremium` helper that uses them.\n\n### APP Mass\nNo conditionals, loops, or invocations were added or removed — the changes were pure renaming and reordering. Mass is **unchanged** (`itemBasePremium` ≈ 9, `quotePremium` ≈ 15). This refactoring targeted **Rule 2 (clarity)**, which trumps APP.\n\n### Rules 3 & 4\n- **No Duplication:** none found.\n- **Fewest Elements:** the `firstInsuranceSurcharge` intermediate was deliberately kept — inlining it would reduce elements but obscure the named 10% surcharge (Rule 2 > Rule 4). No over-engineering added given only 3 passing tests.\n\n### Tests\n**All 3 passing, 34 todo.** Green maintained before and after."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-04-17_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 3\nRecent Green phase: Added COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM (25) and COMPONENT_TYPES set (rune, moonstone), and itemBasePremium helper that returns component base for components else the main-item base premium.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 3\nRecent Green phase: Added COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM (25) and COMPONENT_TYPES set (rune, moonstone), and itemBasePremium helper that returns component base for components else the main-item base premium.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784909241863},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll refactor the implementation. Let me first read the current state of both files."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01D8WqozL9dFDDDYCUYw9JVH","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-04-17_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Ut5TQnEFNkMe8e9FpsVE13","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-04-17_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":240,"output":268,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10212,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909241883,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-abd3ff67-04d5-40cf-b396-0d1538575dc3","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01D8WqozL9dFDDDYCUYw9JVH","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst itemBasePremium = (item: Item): number =>\n  COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)\n    ? COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM\n    : BASE_PREMIUM[item.type];\n\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE = 0.1;\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: QuoteStep[];\n}\n\nconst quotePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const policyBase = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + itemBasePremium(item),\n    0,\n  );\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE;\n  return policyBase + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE;\n};\n\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): { results: unknown[] } => {\n  const results = scenario.steps.map((step) => ({\n    premium: quotePremium(step.items),\n  }));\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909244857},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Ut5TQnEFNkMe8e9FpsVE13","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Base premiums / simplest cases ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n  it(\"single sword (base 100) newcomer first insurance -> 100 + 10 first + 5 fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Building block of 3 alike components (base premiums) ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> base premium 50 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    // base 50 + 10% first (5) + fee 5 = 60\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 60 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"3 runes -> base premium 60 G (block applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"4 runes -> base premium 100 G (no block; block requires exactly 3)\");\n  it.todo(\"7 runes -> base premium 175 G\");\n\n  // --- 'Alike' components ---\n  it.todo(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> base premium 75 G (no block: different types)\");\n  it.todo(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> base premium 120 G (two separate blocks)\");\n\n  // --- Item base premiums for all main items ---\n  it.todo(\"amulet base premium 60 G\");\n  it.todo(\"staff base premium 80 G\");\n  it.todo(\"potion base premium 40 G\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword (100) + plain amulet (60): base 160, curse adds 50 (of sword only) -> 210 before further modifiers and fee\");\n\n  // --- Modifier thresholds ---\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years -> loyalty discount applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword enchantment 5 and cursed -> both surcharges apply\");\n  it.todo(\"sword enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge; curse only if cursed\");\n\n  // --- Integration examples ---\n  it.todo(\"newcomer with cursed sword (steel, ench 3): premium 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"long-standing (3y) 2nd contract, cursed sword (steel, ench 7): premium 160 G; first insurance still applies per item\");\n\n  // --- Rounding ---\n  it.todo(\"premium yielding 197.5 G -> 198 G (rounded up, MHPCO favor)\");\n  it.todo(\"payout yielding 350.5 G -> 350 G (rounded down, MHPCO favor)\");\n\n  // --- Claim: standard reimbursement ---\n  it.todo(\"regular sword (steel, ench 3), damage 500 -> payout 400 (full minus 100 deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"rune damage 200 -> payout 100 (full minus deductible; no special clause)\");\n\n  // --- Claim: enchantment threshold vs dragon material ---\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword ench 8, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (50% clause then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (both apply, 50% wins, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword ench 5, damage 800 -> payout 700 (dragon full reimbursement, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"steel sword ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (high-enchantment 50% then deductible)\");\n\n  // --- Claim: deductible per damage event ---\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack damages sword (500) and amulet (300) -> payout 600 (deductible once per item)\");\n\n  // --- Multiple items of the same type ---\n  it.todo(\"policy covers two swords -> insurance sum 2000, cap 4000\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack damages both swords -> each entry separate damage with own deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"more damages of a type than covered (2 sword damages, 1 sword insured) -> claim rejected (error)\");\n\n  // --- Cap / insurance sum ---\n  it.todo(\"policy covers sword and amulet -> insurance sum 1600, cap 3200\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword (premium modifiers) -> cap 2000 (based on unmodified insurance value)\");\n  it.todo(\"policy covers sword and 3 runes (block) -> insurance sum 1750 (block affects premium only)\");\n  it.todo(\"sword (cap 2000), two claims of 1500: first payout 1400 remaining 600; second payout 600 remaining 0\");\n\n  // --- Edge cases ---\n  it.todo(\"quote with unknown item type -> non-zero exit / error\");\n  it.todo(\"claim references item not in policy -> error\");\n  it.todo(\"claim damage amount -200 -> error\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909244857},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me run the tests to confirm they're green before refactoring."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01RAiN7ngwB3s5NisEVZx