ing Applied — Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) + Rule 3 (No Duplication):**\n\nRestructured `policyBasePremium` to name the partition explicitly:\n\n```ts\n// Before: inline chained filter/reduce + separate filter for count\nconst mainItemsBase = items\n  .filter((item) => !isComponent(item))\n  .reduce((sum, item) => sum + MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM[item.type], 0);\nconst componentCount = items.filter(isComponent).length;\n\n// After: named partition, reduce operates on the smaller mainItems set\nconst components = items.filter(isComponent);\nconst mainItems = items.filter((item) => !isComponent(item));\nconst mainItemsBase = mainItems.reduce(\n  (sum, item) => sum + MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM[item.type],\n  0,\n);\nreturn mainItemsBase + componentGroupBasePremium(components.length);\n```\n\n**Why:** The function's core concept is *\"split policy items into main items vs. components, then price each group.\"* Naming `components` and `mainItems` makes that partition self-documenting, and the reduce now runs over the already-filtered `mainItems` rather than re-filtering inline — surfacing the two-group structure clearly.\n\n**APP Mass:** Roughly neutral (~45; two named bindings added, one intermediate `componentCount` binding removed and folded into `components.length`). Per the guidelines, **Rule 2 (clarity) trumps APP** — the marginal mass change is justified by clearer intent.\n\n**Mass Change:** ~45 → ~45 (neutral; clarity improvement prioritized)\n\n**Tests:** All 4 passing, 33 todo."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-04-17_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 4\nRecent Green phase: Added block pricing for components: componentGroupBasePremium returns BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM (60) when exactly BLOC