irstInsuranceSurcharge` — clear explaining variable. ✓\n\nNaming is already strong. No renames needed.\n\n### Step 2: Rule Evaluation\n\n**Rule 1 (Tests Pass):** All 6 pass. ✓\n\n**Rule 2 (Reveals Intent):** One weakness — `runScenario` returns `{ results: unknown[] }`. The `unknown[]` hides the actual shape (`{ premium }`). A named result type would reveal intent.\n\n**Rule 3 (No Duplication):** No duplication found.\n\n**Rule 4 (Fewest Elements):** The code is already minimal. `policyBasePremium` filters twice, but splitting components vs. main items keeps intent clear (Rule 2 trumps micro-optimization).\n\n### Step 3: Chosen Refactoring\n\nReplace `unknown[]` with an explicit `QuoteResult` type — improves Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) with negligible APP cost.\n\n### Step 4: APP Mass — Return Type Region\n\nThe `unknown[]` region carries no runtime mass (types are erased), but the returned object shape gains clarity. This is a pure Rule-2 improvement; APP mass of executable code is unchanged (bindings/invocations identical).\n\nLet me apply it:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01RGvukmAmNsTetA9N3R7Fdw","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"export const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): { results: unknown[] } => {\n  const results = scenario.steps.map((step) => ({\n    premium: quotePremium(step.items),\n  }));\n  return { results };\n};","newText":"interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport const runScenario = (\n  scenario: Scenario,\n): { results: QuoteResult[] } => {\n  const results = scenario.steps.map((step) => ({\n    premium: quotePremium(step.items),\n  }));\n  return { results };\n};"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":3682,"output":1365,"cacheRead":9900,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14947,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909410530,"responseI