all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":943,"output":231,"cacheRead":40113,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":41287,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909457187,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-4d8fe385-b9c2-4f23-a2c2-0c25e9f47b84","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01MGzRqngbFJUYDN4jL8ZzzS","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 7 tests still pass.\n\n### Step 5: New APP Mass (refactored components portion)\n\n```\nconst componentsBase = [...countByType(components).values()].reduce(  // binding(1)+invocation values(2)+invocation reduce(2)+spread(~1) = ~6\n  (sum, count) => sum + componentGroupBasePremium(count),  // bindings(2)+invocation(2)+add(1) = 5\n  0,  // constant(1)\n);\n```\nSubtotal ≈ **12** (was ~25). The grouping logic moved into the reusable, single-concept `countByType` helper (its internal loop mass is unchanged but now isolated and named).\n\nNet effect: removed the mutable `let componentsBase = 0` + `+=` loop (2 assignments, 6 each) in favor of a single declarative `reduce` — eliminating 2 mutations and unifying both sums on the same idiom.\n\n### Step 6: Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Unified both premium sums on the declarative `reduce` idiom (previously `mainItemsBase` used `reduce` while `componentsBase` used a mutable `let` + `for` loop). Consistency improves readability.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: Extracted `countByType` — a single, named representation of the \"count occurrences by type\" concept, separating grouping from pricing.\n- **Rule 4 / APP**: Removed two mutations (`let componentsBase = 0` and `+=`), lowering mass of the summation section (~25 → ~12).\n\n**Naming**: Evaluated all functions first; `countByType` added with an intent-revealing name; no existing names required changes.\n\n### Step 7: Report\n\n**Refactoring Complete**:\n- **Refactoring**: Extracted `countByType` grouping helper; replaced mutable accumulator loop with declarative `reduce` to match the existing `mainItemsBase` style.\n- **Mass Change**: components-summing section ~25 → ~12 (removed 2 mutations).\n- **Tests**: All 7 passing (30 todo)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-04-17_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 7\nRecent Green phase: policyBasePremium now groups components by type into a Map and applies block pricing per type group.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 7\nRecent Green phase: policyBasePremium now groups components by type into a Map and applies block pricing per type group.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784909462441},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll start by reading the current implementation and test files."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_017Wn4uhV2a7Endd5KzBujdX","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_012x5utMtsvQVuKvSuz3rDmf","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":198,"output":123,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10025,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909462461,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ccadcb20-a8a7-42be-b026-301e604e239f","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_017Wn4uhV2a7Endd5KzBujdX","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"interface Item {\n  type: string;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: QuoteStep[];\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE = 0.1;\n\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst isComponent = (item: Item): boolean => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type);\n\nconst componentGroupBasePremium = (count: number): number => {\n  if (count === BLOCK_SIZE) return BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  return count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n};\n\nconst policyBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const components = items.filter(isComponent);\n  const mainItems = items.filter((item) => !isComponent(item));\n  const mainItemsBase = mainItems.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM[item.type],\n    0,\n  );\n  const componentsByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const component of components) {\n    componentsByType.set(\n      component.type,\n      (componentsByType.get(component.type) ?? 0) + 1,\n    );\n  }\n  let componentsBase = 0;\n  for (const count of componentsByType.values()) {\n    componentsBase += componentGroupBasePremium(count);\n  }\n  return mainItemsBase + componentsBase;\n};\n\nconst quotePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const policyBase = policyBasePremium(items);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE;\n  return Math.ceil(policyBase + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\ninterface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport const runScenario = (\n  scenario: Scenario,\n): { results: QuoteResult[] } => {\n  const results = scenario.steps.map((step) => ({\n    premium: quotePremium(step.items),\n  }));\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909464302},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_012x5utMtsvQVuKvSuz3rDmf","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Base premiums / simplest cases ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n  it(\"single sword (base 100) newcomer first insurance -> 100 + 10 first + 5 fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Building block of 3 alike components (base premiums) ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> base premium 50 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    // base 50 + 10% first (5) + fee 5 = 60\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 60 });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> base premium 60 G (block applies)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // base 60 + 10% first (6) + fee 5 = 71\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> base premium 100 G (no block; block requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // base 100 + 10% first (10) + fee 5 = 115\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> base premium 175 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // base 175 + 10% first (17.5) + fee 5 = 197.5 -> rounded up to 198\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 198 });\n  });\n\n  // --- 'Alike' components ---\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> base premium 75 G (no block: different types)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // base 75 + 10% first (7.5) + fee 5 = 87.5 -> 88\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 88 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> base premium 120 G (two separate blocks)\");\n\n  // --- Item base premiums for all main items ---\n  it.todo(\"amulet base premium 60 G\");\n  it.todo(\"staff base premium 80 G\");\n  it.todo(\"potion base premium 40 G\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword (100) + plain amulet (60): base 160, curse adds 50 (of sword only) -> 210 before further modifiers and fee\");\n\n  // --- Modifier thresholds ---\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years -> loyalty discount applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword enchantment 5 and cursed -> both surcharges apply\");\n  it.todo(\"sword enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge; curse only if cursed\");\n\n  // --- Integration examples ---\n  it.todo(\"newcomer with cursed sword (steel, ench 3): premium 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"long-standing (3y) 2nd contract, cursed sword (steel, ench 7): premium 160 G; first insurance still applies per item\");\n\n  // --- Rounding ---\n  it.todo(\"premium yielding 197.5 G -> 198 G (rounded up, MHPCO favor)\");\n  it.todo(\"payout yielding 350.5 G -> 350 G (rounded down, MHPCO favor)\");\n\n  // --- Claim: standard reimbursement ---\n  it.todo(\"regular sword (steel, ench 3), damage 500 -> payout 400 (full minus 100 deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"rune damage 200 -> payout 100 (full minus deductible; no special clause)\");\n\n  // --- Claim: enchantment threshold vs dragon material ---\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword ench 8, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (50% clause then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (both apply, 50% wins, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword ench 5, damage 800 -> payout 700 (dragon full reimbursement, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"steel sword ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (high-enchantment 50% then deductible)\");\n\n  // --- Claim: deductible per damage event ---\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack damages sword (500) and amulet (300) -> payout 600 (deductible once per item)\");\n\n  // --- Multiple items of the same type ---\n  it.todo(\"policy covers two swords -> insurance sum 2000, cap 4000\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack damages both swords -> each entry separate damage with own deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"more damages of a type than covered (2 sword damages, 1 sword insured) -> claim rejected (error)\");\n\n