ntFor(customer, policyBase)`. This mirrors the existing surcharge/discount vocabulary and makes `quotePremium`'s body a clean, linear composition of named participants (`policyBase + itemSurchargeTotal + firstInsuranceSurcharge − loyaltyDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE`). The conditional loyalty logic now has a self-documenting name rather than a raw ternary embedded among the local declarations.\n\n2. **Rule 2 (Naming):** Renamed the local `itemModifiers` → `itemSurchargeTotal`. \"Modifiers\" was ambiguous (modifiers can be discounts or surcharges), whereas the value is strictly a sum of surcharges (`itemSurcharges`). The new name matches the helper it aggregates.\n\n**Naming Evaluation:** All top-level function names (`quotePremium`, `policyBasePremium`, `itemSurcharges`, `componentGroupBasePremium`) already clearly reveal intent — no renames needed there.\n\n**APP Mass — `quotePremium`:**\n- Before: ~26 (8 bindings, 4 invocations=8, 1 conditional=4, 1 loop=5, 1 constant)\n- After: `quotePremium` body drops the ternary (−4 conditional) but gains one invocation (+2) for `loyaltyDiscountFor`; the extracted helper adds ~9 (2 bindings, 1 conditional=4, 1 invocation isn't present, 1 constant, 1 binding-mult). Net total mass is roughly flat (~+1), but the **conditional complexity is moved out of the hot composition path into a single-purpose, testable helper**.\n\nThis is a case where **Rule 2 trumps APP**: the tiny mass increase buys a clearer, more maintainable premium-composition expression consistent with the existing surcharge helpers. All other rules (Rule 3 no duplication, Rule 4 fewest elements) were evaluated — no duplication exists and the abstraction level is appropriate for the growing set of surcharge/discount rules in the pending todos.\n\n**Refactoring:** Extracted `loyaltyDiscountFor` helper; renamed `itemModifiers` → `itemSurchargeTotal`\n**Mass Change:** ~26 → ~27 in `quotePremium` (flat; conditional relocated to focused helper) — clarity gain justifies it per Rule 2\n**Tests:** All 13 passing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-04-17_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 13\nRecent Green phase: Added Customer interface, LOYALTY_DISCOUNT (0.2) and LOYALTY_YEARS (2). quotePremium now takes customer and subtracts a policy-wide loyalty discount when yearsWithMHPCO >= 2.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 13\nRecent Green phase: Added Customer interface, LOYALTY_DISCOUNT (0.2) and LOYALTY_YEARS (2). quotePremium now takes customer and subtracts a policy-wide loyalty discount when yearsWithMHPCO >= 2.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784909676257},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll start by reading the implementation and test files to understand the current state."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01UoPstYshETfGM7ZBhp6P6o","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01NwdZdjn1w3HmTqRyEYC9wt","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":255,"output":128,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10087,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909676277,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-c8d0ca76-50e3-4622-865e-502e99898f98","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01UoPstYshETfGM7ZBhp6P6o","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"interface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: QuoteStep[];\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS = 2;\n\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst isComponent = (item: Item): boolean => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type);\n\nconst componentGroupBasePremium = (count: number): number => {\n  if (count === BLOCK_SIZE) return BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  return count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n};\n\nconst countByType = (items: Item[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE = 0.5;\n\nconst itemBaseFor = (item: Item): number =>\n  isComponent(item)\n    ? COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM\n    : MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM[item.type];\n\nconst itemSurcharges = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = itemBaseFor(item);\n  let surcharge = 0;\n  if (item.cursed) surcharge += base * CURSE_SURCHARGE;\n  return surcharge;\n};\n\nconst policyBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const components = items.filter(isComponent);\n  const mainItems = items.filter((item) => !isComponent(item));\n  const mainItemsBase = mainItems.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + itemBaseFor(item),\n    0,\n  );\n  const componentsBase = [...countByType(components).values()].reduce(\n    (sum, count) => sum + componentGroupBasePremium(count),\n    0,\n  );\n  return mainItemsBase + componentsBase;\n};\n\nconst quotePremium = (items: Item[], customer: Customer): number => {\n  const policyBase = policyBasePremium(items);\n  const itemModifiers = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + itemSurcharges(item),\n    0,\n  );\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE;\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS ? policyBase * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT : 0;\n  return Math.ceil(\n    policyBase +\n      itemModifiers +\n      firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n      loyaltyDiscount +\n      PROCESSING_FEE,\n  );\n};\n\ninterface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport const runScenario = (\n  scenario: Scenario,\n): { results: QuoteResult[] } => {\n  const results = scenario.steps.map((step) => ({\n    premium: quotePremium(step.items, scenario.customer),\n  }));\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909678056},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01NwdZdjn1w3HmTqRyEYC9wt","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Base premiums / simplest cases ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n  it(\"single sword (base 100) newcomer first insurance -> 100 + 10 first + 5 fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Building block of 3 alike components (base premiums) ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> base premium 50 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    // base 50 + 10% first (5) + fee 5 = 60\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 60 });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> base premium 60 G (block applies)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // base 60 + 10% first (6) + fee 5 = 71\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> base premium 100 G (no block; block requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // base 100 + 10% first (10) + fee 5 = 115\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> base premium 175 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // base 175 + 10% first (17.5) + fee 5 = 197.5 -> rounded up to 198\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 198 });\n  });\n\n  // --- 'Alike' components ---\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> base premium 75 G (no block: different types)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // base 75 + 10% first (7.5) + fee 5 = 87.5 -> 88\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 88 });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> base premium 120 G (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // base 120 + 10% first (12) + fee 5 = 137\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 137 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Item base premiums for all main items ---\n  it(\"amulet base premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    // 60 + 6 first + 5 fee = 71\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"staff base premium 80 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    // 80 + 8 first + 5 fee = 93\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 93 });\n  });\n  it(\"potion base premium 40 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    // 40 + 4 first + 5 fee = 49\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 49 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it(\"cursed sword (100) + plain amulet (60): base 160, curse adds 50 (of sword only) -> 210 before further modifiers and fee\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"sword\", cursed: true },\n            { type: \"amulet\", cursed: false },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // policy base 160 + curse 50 = 210; + first 16 (10% of 160) + fee 5 = 231\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 231 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Modifier thresholds ---\n  it(\"customer with exactly 2 years -> loyalty discount applies\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    // base 100 - loyalty 20 (20%) + first 10 (10%) + fee 5 = 95\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 95 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword enchantment 5 and cursed -> both surcharges apply\");\n  it.todo(\"sword enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge; curse only if cursed\");\n\n  // --- Integration examples ---\n  it.todo(\"newcomer with cursed sword (steel, ench 3): premium 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"long-standing (3y) 2nd contract, cursed sword (steel, ench 7): premium 160 G; first insurance still applies per item\");\n\n  // --- Rounding ---\n  it.todo(\"premium yielding 197.5 G -> 198 G (rounded up, MHPCO favor)\");\n  it.todo(\"payout yielding 350.5 G -> 350 G (rounded down, MHPCO favor)\");\n\n  // --- Claim: standard reimbursement ---\n  it.todo(\"regular sword (steel, ench 3), damage 500 -> payout 400 (full minus 100 deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"rune damage 200 -> payout 100 (full minus deductible; no special clause)\");\n\n  // --- Claim: enchantment threshold vs dragon material ---\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword ench 8, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (50% clause then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (both apply, 50% wins, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword ench 5, damage 800 -> payout 700 (dragon full reimbursement, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"steel sword ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (high-enchantment 50% then deductible)\");\n\n  // --- Claim: deductible per damage event ---\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack damages sword (500) and amulet (300) -> payout 600 (deductible once per item)\");\n\n  // --- Multiple items of the same type ---\n  it.todo(\"policy covers two swords -> insurance sum 2000, cap 4000\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack damages both swords -> each entry separate damage with own deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"more damages of a type than covered (2 sword damages, 1 sword insured) -> claim rejected (error)\");\n\n  // --- Cap / insurance sum ---\n  it.todo(\"policy covers sword and amulet -> insurance sum 1600, cap 3200\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword (premium modifiers) -> cap 2000 (based on unmodified insurance value)\");\n  it.todo(\"policy covers sword and 3 runes (block) -> insurance sum 1750 (block affects premium only)\");\n  it.todo(\"sword (cap 2000), two claims of 1500: first payout 1400 remaining 600; second payout 600 remaining 0\");\n\n  // --- Edge cases ---\n  it.todo(\"quote with unknown item type -> non-zero exit / error\");\n  it.todo(\"claim references item not in policy -> error\");\n  it.todo(\"claim damage amount -200 -> error\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909678056},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Running the tests to verify everything works as expected.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me run the tests to confirm the baseline."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01CqdUZJ77oREWAYRC6fpDqo","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-04-17_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":5049,"output":167,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14920,"cost":{"input":0