,{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Green Phase Complete: 30 passing, tsc clean."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01PQkdS7muMSG55YVEW42ApQ","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 30\nRecent Green phase: processClaim now validates that the number of damages of each itemType does not exceed the number of insured items of that type, throwing an Error if exceeded (using countByType on covered items and on damages).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":971,"output":267,"cacheRead":89928,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":91166,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784910230732,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-3dd0ea21-40db-4bc5-8f15-b4f9634733d0","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01PQkdS7muMSG55YVEW42ApQ","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 30 tests remain green.\n\n### Step 5: New APP Mass\n\nThe validation logic is unchanged in composition — it now lives in a named function. `processClaim` gains one invocation (`assertDamagesWithinCoverage`) but sheds the inline guard block.\n\n```\nprocessClaim guard portion after:\n- assertDamagesWithinCoverage(...) invocation = 2\n\nExtracted function assertDamagesWithinCoverage body: 36 (same as before, relocated)\n\nNet local mass change in processClaim: 36 -> 2 (guard concern moved out)\nExtracted helper: +36 (but now isolated, named, single-responsibility)\nWhole-file mass: unchanged (~0 net; +2 for the call site, +named params)\n```\n\nThe whole-file APP mass is essentially neutral (a single added invocation of +2). This is intentional: **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps APP**. The refactoring trades a negligible mass increase for a substantial clarity gain.\n\n### Step 6: Decision\n\n```\nRefactoring Applied:\n- Naming: Extracted inline damage-count guard into `assertDamagesWithinCoverage`\n  — the name states exactly what the guard enforces.\n- Rule 2 (Reveals Intent): processClaim now reads as three clear intentions:\n  assert coverage → compute payout → compute cap. The \"guard\" concern is\n  named and separated from the \"compute\" concern.\n- Rule 3: No new duplication; countByType still reused.\n- Rule 4: No unnecessary elements introduced; one focused helper.\n- Mass: whole-file essentially neutral (+2 for the extracted call site);\n  clarity deliberately prioritized over raw mass per APP guidance.\n\nBenefits:\n- processClaim is now a readable pipeline of named steps.\n- The validation rule is independently testable and reusable.\n- Single-responsibility per function.\n```\n\n### Step 7: Report\n\n```\nRefactoring Complete:\nRefactoring: Extracted damage-coverage validation from processClaim into a\n             named assertDamagesWithinCoverage helper (Rule 2: Reveals Intent).\nMass Change: whole-file neutral (+2 call site); clarity prioritized over mass.\nTests: All 30 passing (7 todo).\n```"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-04-17_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 30\nRecent Green phase: processClaim now validates that the number of damages of each itemType does not exceed the number of insured items of that type, throwing an Error if exceeded (using countByType on covered items and on damages).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously,